title Caravan fence -- a phase follows a prefix of its turn, and a prefix is one number
prompt Keaton set the autonomous loop running: read the canon and the card, close open reds first, then take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first and send it as its own signed round.
think Standfast first. The REDS ledger reads clean -- 84, 85 (reopened and closed), 86, 87 all released -- and the living-card ASCII witness ran GREEN on metal this lap before any new work opened, so the line was not stopped.
think The thread is the Microkernel Target, Equinox 1, and the crux was already named by the last lap's own recommend rather than invented here: the link phases.rye seated orders a turn's phases TOTALLY, which is stronger than most turns need, and a turn whose middle phases are genuinely independent pays for an order it never asked for. The question was whether a phase may name what it depends on without the queue growing a graph a supervisor has to walk.
think The refusal came before the design. A dependency list is a graph, and a graph means walking edges and closing them transitively at every admission -- a supervisor whose admission cost climbs with the turn is a different machine from the one this arc built. So the shape had to be one that needs no closure computed.
think A prefix is that shape. One number per phase: how many leading phases of its own turn it follows. The relation is transitively closed by construction, because a prefix already holds every prefix inside it -- if this phase follows steps 0..after-1 and one of those follows a third, that third is already inside this prefix. One integer comparison, no walk, no visited set.
think The elder reading falls out as a special case rather than a rival: after = step is the link exactly, and the selftest proves that pair by pair over the whole lap rather than asserting it in prose. after = 0 frees a phase of its siblings entirely.
think The lap needed both effects at once or the finding would have been half-honest. A fence that only frees is no fence; a fence that only binds is the link. So the last turn carries one of each -- a peek at menu under a fence of zero, free to pass its blocked sibling, and a peek at back_b under a fence of two, held behind both.
think Reuse over restatement held again. cut() hands a phases.Phase to phases.items_contend and phases.plan_is_ordered for every question this rung does not change, so the three readings' numbers stand beside the elder rungs unconverted, and the fenced reading differs from the linked one in exactly one clause.
think One walk answers both measures. sibling_waits takes the prefix as a parameter -- plan[pick].step weighs every earlier sibling, which is the link's own question, and plan[pick].after weighs the prefix the phase actually named -- so out_of_turn and out_of_fence come from one function called twice rather than two near-identical walks.
obs The numbers say it in one line: slots unspent read 7 by act, 8 fenced, 10 linked. The fence sits exactly between, which is the whole claim. Passes 2 / 1 / 0 and phases run past their turn 2 / 1 / 0 say the same thing from the other side, and the fence is broken 1 time by act and 0 fenced.
obs The gain is lawful rather than loose. The fenced reading runs 1 phase past its turn where the link runs 0, and that is not a violation -- the author wrote that freedom down. What the fence never does is break a prefix somebody named: 0, under its own invariant, on metal.
obs Both RED paths proven on metal before any GREEN claim. Drop the fence from items_contend and the pure read reds at a phase inside a named prefix being free to pass it -- caught in the happy zone, before a single child starts. Keep the fence and hide it from the choosing alone, and the fenced run's own fill_table invariant fires at fence.rye.zig:442, so the assert saying a fenced reading never runs a phase past its named prefix is load-bearing rather than decorative.
obs The isolation half needed nothing here either, and for the reason phases.rye already gave: two phases of one turn share a domain, and commute.admissible refuses to stand a domain beside itself. A fence loosens an order and opens no instant.
obs Council rota lap 472 mod 27 = 13 -- the happy zone and the thin edge, read deep. It shaped the file's own division directly: check_fence is a pure fold over the declaration and the plan, instant, no child started and no store touched, and it caught the first RED before the thin edge ever ran; check_order is the thin edge, where only real processes can tell the truth. The multiplication collapsed into an addition exactly as the teaching promises.
obs Thirty-two green-witnessed Rye rings now carry the Microkit shape across real processes. TAME surface GREEN -- style bans clean, width-check exit 0 -- and the neighbor rung re-GREEN: caravan_phases_witness passed unchanged beside the new one.
loom witness=caravan_fence_witness children=6 passes_by_act=2 passes_fenced=1 passes_linked=0 slots_unspent_by_act=7 slots_unspent_fenced=8 slots_unspent_linked=10 out_of_turn_fenced=1 out_of_fence_fenced=0
file caravan/fence.rye the rung -- a phase names one number, and a prefix needs no graph
file tools/caravan_fence_witness.rish the witness on metal, three readings over one lap
file caravan/README.md the durable entry beside its elder rungs
file crux/REMEMBER.md the live edge moved forward, the elder edge folded to a pointer
recommend keep-going the honest next crux is what a prefix still cannot express -- a fence orders a phase against a contiguous run of its own turn, so a phase genuinely independent of step 0 yet dependent on step 1 must name both or neither, and the question becomes whether that gap is worth a second number (a window rather than a prefix) or whether it is the price of never walking a graph, which wants a lap measuring how often real turns actually want the hole
